fix(v4): stop the object JIT fastpass keeping a swallowed issue's value (#6407) fix(v4): stop the object JIT fastpass keeping a swallowed issue's value (#6407)

The `optin`/`optout`-optional codegen branch suppressed the issue on an
absent key but still ran the assignment, so a value written by a failing
check landed in a successful result:

    const schema = z.object({
      a: z.string().optional().superRefine((_v, ctx) => {
        ctx.addIssue({ code: "custom", message: "bad" });
        ctx.value = "leaked";
      }),
    });

    schema.safeParse({});                    // { success: true, data: { a: "leaked" } }
    schema.safeParse({}, { jitless: true }); // { success: true, data: {} }

The interpreted path returns early in the same situation and async goes
through it, so the divergence was JIT only.

While here, collapse the identical arms of the required-in branch's
assignment — it shrinks the generated source by four lines per key.
